--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. fegone/claude-code-delegate-local  -- MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Felix Gonzalez
   https://github.com/fegone/claude-code-delegate-local

   The primary ancestor. Ported from it, in adapted and re-authored form:
     - the agentic turn loop and its turn/nudge accounting
     - three-tier agent lookup and frontmatter parsing
     - workdir-confined path resolution
     - the subprocess environment allowlist
     - tool-result eviction (context pruning)
     - duplicate-tool-call de-duplication
     - read_file pagination and run_bash output truncation markers
     - retry/backoff with Retry-After handling
     - turn-countdown injection and the final-turn short-circuit
     - real-exit-code capture, and the test that polices it
     - the Anthropic-shaped canonical message representation

   All model-facing strings (tool descriptions, error messages returned to the
   delegated model) were re-authored in English; upstream's are Spanish. This is
   a functional change, not a translation of comments.

2. mixicz/claude-code-delegate-local  -- MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Felix Gonzalez
   https://github.com/mixicz/claude-code-delegate-local
   (a fork of 1; its LICENSE is unchanged from upstream, so its additions carry
   the same notice)

   Ported from it, in adapted form:
     - agent frontmatter actually binding the dispatch
     - per-agent reasoning-effort resolution with fail-loud validation
     - per-agent tool restriction enforced at both declaration and execution
     - the workdir-root allowlist
     - the bubblewrap run_bash sandbox: empty-root design, bind-order rules,
       HOME literal-vs-realpath handling, and the network toggle

3. fjgbue/claude-delegator-deepseek-mcp  -- see that repository for its terms
   https://github.com/fjgbue/claude-delegator-deepseek-mcp

   No code was taken. The `files[]` server-side context-prefetch *idea* comes
   from here; this implementation was written independently and differs
   materially (total-byte budget, binary detection, secret denylist,
   skip-whole-files-rather-than-truncate).

